  "pass_a_gloss": "If divine words exist in the Law, Prophets, Gospels, and Apostles, a disciple must recognize God as the teacher, for God is the one who teaches knowledge, as written in Psalms. The Savior testifies that no one should be called a teacher on earth, for there is one teacher, the Father in heaven, who teaches either through Himself, Christ, the Holy Spirit, or the apostles, but only God's Spirit and Word should dwell and teach. What is this said for? Because the prophet says, 'Reveal Yourself to me, Lord, that I may know,' for I will not know unless You reveal Yourself, and when You reveal Yourself, I will see their deeds and understand each person's actions and choices.",
